.TH LIBKECCAK_K12_UPDATE 3 LIBKECCAK
.SH NAME
libkeccak_k12_update - absorb the next message chunk into a KT128 context
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <libkeccak/k12.h>

int libkeccak_k12_update(struct libkeccak_k12 *\fIctx\fP, const void *\fIdata\fP, size_t \fIlength\fP);
.fi
.PP
Link with
.IR -lkeccak .
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.BR libkeccak_k12_update ()
function absorbs
.I length
message bytes from
.IR data .
It may be called any number of times before
.BR libkeccak_k12_final (3);
how the message is split across calls does not change the result.
Zero-length updates are permitted, and NUL bytes are ordinary data.
The buffer is only borrowed for the duration of the call and may be
reused or overwritten once it returns. A NULL
.I data
pointer is accepted only when
.I length
is zero.
.SH RETURN VALUES
The function returns 0 on success and -1 on error. It fails if
.I ctx
is NULL, if the context has already been finalised, or if
.I data
is NULL with a non-zero
.IR length .
A failed call does not alter the context.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libkeccak_k12_create (3),
.BR libkeccak_k12_final (3),
.BR libkeccak_k12 (7)
